+# Apple III profile
+
+`iigs_disk` also handles WOZ-capable Apple-III cores (S0 advertises WOZ).
+Older Apple-III builds keep their existing generic image path.
+
+- S0: internal Disk III (.D1).
+- S1: first external Disk III (.D2).
+- S2/S3: raw block-device payloads, read-only. The current FPGA exposes only
+  S0/S1; these assignments reserve the block-device interface without treating
+  S1 as the Apple //e hard-disk slot.
+
+The shared 5.25 encoder uses proper 10-bit sync words. Apple III's profile adds
+its standard synchronized track rotation and SOS address-field key from tracks
+9–16. These are reconstructed only for sector sources. Native WOZ is validated
+and served unchanged; NIB preserves its address fields and data bytes.
+
+Apple III converted images and block payloads are read-only. Native WOZ2
+bitstream files permit writes within existing track allocations. Main preserves
+metadata and unrelated chunks, clears CRC to zero before the first write, and
+rejects writes outside those allocations. WOZ1, FLUX, archives and protected
+images remain read-only. No reverse sector conversion occurs for Apple III.
+
+The hardware still implements Apple III's P6 sequencer, independent spindle/I/O
+selection, motor timeout, disk-change latch and physical bit timing. Main handles
+file formats and file I/O via the existing SD protocol, including multi-block
+transfers up to 16 KiB. No new FPGA/Main transport protocol is introduced.
+
+`tests/apple3/run.sh` exercises the shared backend, including //e/IIgs
+regressions. The Apple III core's simulator exercises the real-time disk path
+using the same converted WOZ output.
